/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 75 0 R
/E (Kenya should leverage the Data Protection Act of 20192 by issuing sector-specific guidance that requires explicit, informed parental consent for classroom recordings. Education authorities should move from reactive penalties to proactive digital-literacy campaigns that train teachers in data hygiene, viral-content risks, and cyber-extortion, while encouraging safe educational use that protects student dignity and avoids using students as props for personal brand-building.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [0 2 1]
>>
